            <ArticleTitle>Coronary angioplasty for coronary stenosis after the arterial switch procedure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>621-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary balloon angioplasty seems to be an adequate therapy for proximal coronary stenoses developing after the arterial switch operation, with adequate medium-term results. Overexpansion of the lesion seems to be necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
